\\begin{aligned}T(u) & =0 \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}10\\cdot k+6\\cdot 5 \\\\ 25\\cdot k+15\\cdot 5\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}10k+30 \\\\ 25k+75\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}10k+30=0 \\\\ 25k+75=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution to both of these equations is $k=-3.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186366359 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186366360 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186366359 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186366361 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186366359 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186366362 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186366359 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186366363 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186366359 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186366364 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186366359 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186366359 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186366359 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186366363 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186366359 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "5d2a5091-37af-5723-bdf8-06f99b82a475" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186366360 #edb/ref 1080 "3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186366360 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186366360 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "dc2731d7-9bf4-59e2-a5fd-0d22940726ec" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186366361 #edb/ref 1080 "2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186366361 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186366361 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "709deace-e72b-54bb-b36d-e6919d9318f2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186366362 #edb/ref 1080 "-4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186366362 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186366362 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "fb1e702e-0eca-5685-a172-661e4405d724" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186366363 #edb/ref 1080 "-3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186366363 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186366363 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "bc073656-5139-5cae-8a20-3b10563f43e3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186366364 #edb/ref 1080 "-2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186366364 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186366364 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "c03c8cfa-dd96-52a1-98a2-b3436e3bfde5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394037 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186394038 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394037 #edb/ref 1069 "q-80671" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394037 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394037 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the linear transformation $T:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}3x+y+3z \\\\ 2x+y+z \\\\ x-y+5z\\end{aligned}]$ and the vector $\\,u=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ k\\end{aligned}].$ Find the value of $\\,k\\,$ such that $\\,u\\in \\text{Ker}(T).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394037 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "a4dce28d-b322-5c7f-88fd-a0c01e48564e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394037 #edb/ref 1074 "A vector $u$ belongs to the kernel of a linear transformation $T$ if $T(u)=0.$ \n\nSo, we need to solve the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(u) & =0 \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}3\\cdot (-2)+3+3\\cdot k \\\\ 2\\cdot (-2)+3+k \\\\ -2-3+5\\cdot k\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}-3+3k \\\\ -1+k \\\\ -5+5k\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-3+3k=0 \\\\ -1+k=0 \\\\ -5+5k=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution to all three of these equations is $k=1.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394038 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186394039 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394038 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186394040 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394038 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186394041 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394038 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186394042 #edb/