f 17592186045417] [17592186419578 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186419553 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186419578 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "e00646f1-87a0-5a44-9d32-d7268a416e97" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186419579 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186419574 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186419579 #edb/ref 1069 "q-140056" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186419579 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186419579 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the linear transformation $T:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}2x+4y-2z \\\\ -3x-6y+3z \\\\ 4x+8y-4z\\end{aligned}].$ Find $\\,\\text{Ker}(T).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186419579 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "32b7b7cc-73cb-5678-9200-bd4242fb8265" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186419579 #edb/ref 1074 "Finding the kernel of $T$ is equivalent to finding the null space of the standard matrix of $T.$\n\nFror the given linear transformation, the standard matrix is $T=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 & -2 \\\\ -3 & -6 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 8 & -4\\end{aligned}].$ \n\nSetting $x=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],$ we then need to solve the equation $Tx=0.$ First, we find reduce $T$ to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 & -2 \\\\ -3 & -6 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 8 & -4\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(\\frac{3}{2}){R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 8 & -4\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variable is $x$, and we have two free variables, $y,$ and $z.$ That means we need to find $x$ in terms of $y$ and $z.$ \n\nFrom the first equation, we get \n\n$$\nx=-2y+z.\n$$\n\n  \n\nTherefore, the kernel of the linear transformation $\\,T$ is ${[\\begin{aligned}-2y+z \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,y,z\\in R}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186419584 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186419586 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186419584 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "3d23af43-be13-585f-9055-f003ed10a6af" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186419584 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186419580 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186419585 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186419587 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186419585 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "acaaf24c-b820-5d27-9cad-c26f7f900e0e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186419585 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186419583 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186419586 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "e5b6668f-23d9-5bd7-ab9f-9383a9c47d8d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186419586 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186419579 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186419587 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186419588 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186419587 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "f4e671bf-aca9-5c31-b460-2f7da409a479" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186419587 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186419582 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186419588 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186419584 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186419588 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "fa869ace-3a7c-544c-91f1-9f8e4eedf28f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186419588 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186419581 #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
